Q: what is free cash flow
 -> Free cash flow is the cash a company generates from its operations after subtracting capital expenditures — the money left over to pay down debt, return to shareholders, or reinvest in the business. It's often seen as a cleaner measure of financial health than net income because it's harder to manipulate with accounting choices.

